# Fixture: local-playing. The tour every artboard width is captured through.
# Widths come from the driver (REDSHANK_WIDTH/HEIGHT), never from here.
settle 30
assert snap item-count >= 1
capture listen

# The dock must actually be playing: a run that never reached the device or
# the source is not a receipt of anything. From the start, because the fixture
# is two seconds long and a saved position near its end completes at once.
act seek:0
act play
# Fifteen frames, not five: a seek on a range-served item costs a request
# before play applies, and the dock reads PAUSED until it does. Five frames
# passed or failed with the machine's frame rate (2026-09-23). Fifteen still
# ends far inside the two-second fixture.
settle 15
assert snap transport ~ PLAYING
settle 5
capture listen-playing
act pause
settle 10
capture listen-paused

act tab:library
settle 10
assert snap tab == Library
capture library

act tab:notes
settle 10
assert snap tab == Notes
capture notes
act notes:all
settle 5
capture notes-all
act notes:this
settle 5

act tab:mere
settle 10
assert snap tab == Mere
capture mere-chain
act scene:orrery
settle 10
assert snap scene == orrery
capture mere-orrery
act scene:trail
settle 10
capture mere-trail
act scene:chain
settle 5

act tab:settings
settle 10
assert snap tab == Settings
capture settings

# Family B: the same facts on the left rail.
act tab:listen
act layout:rail
settle 15
assert snap layout == rail
capture rail
act layout:dock
settle 10

# The brand shell is a scope class, not a second markup.
act seed:brand
settle 10
assert snap seed == brand
capture brand
act mode:light
settle 10
assert snap mode == light
capture brand-light
act mode:hc-dark
settle 10
capture brand-hc-dark
act seed:wetland
act mode:dark
settle 10
log listen_playing complete
